    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U05-L04-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "4.3: Reflecting Across a Different Way",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Considering first the equation \\(g(x)=\\text-f(x)\\), we know that for the same input \\(x\\), the value of \\(g(x)\\) will be the opposite of the value of \\(f(x)\\). For example, since \\(f(0)=1\\), we know that \\(g(0)=\\text-f(0)=\\text-1\\). We can…",
